The paper supports the construction, with one correction to the retained write-up: the intersection formula is Lemma 2.4, not Lemma 2.5; Lemma 3.1 supplies primariness when the radical sum is prime. I also found two audit issues in the measurements: 0 hits in 200,000 samples is not by itself proof of a sub-\(10^{-6}\) probability (the exact root-pair density is available), and the “reference” scan was needlessly doing huge-integer Horner arithmetic at every candidate instead of exact modular rejection followed by exact confirmation. I’m fixing both before rerunning the gates.
