codex
One more gate-level correction is needed before the oracle run: at degree 72, the advertised 34-operation shortcut omitted the exact Horner confirmations a solver should perform. Counting multiplication and addition separately puts the honest route at 326 operations, over G9(c). I’m lowering only the hard preset’s degree to 64 while keeping the 75,000-root haystack; the witness stays fixed-size, the exact guess density improves, and the full derive-plus-confirm route is 296 operations.
